      en: "Vaitape Harbor is the main port of entry for Bora Bora's tourism industry. The harbor was first built in the 1940s by the US military during WWII as a seaplane base. Today, it handles the majority of supplies for the island's luxury resorts. The harbor has a dedicated fuel dock supplying diesel and gasoline. It also serves as a base for scientific vessels studying coral reefs. The local economy is heavily dependent on the harbor; a strike in 2020 caused a 40% drop in tourist arrivals. Security measures include CCTV and a 24/7 harbor master. The port authority enforces strict environmental standards, such as waste disposal from ships. Plans for a marina expansion were approved in 2023 to accommodate superyachts.",
